WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 8.5 · Marketing & Communications
Website, SEO and discoverability

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Your website is where people check you are real and trustworthy; one good page can be enough to start.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:26.652
Your website is often where people check whether you are real, relevant and trustworthy. Discoverability means people can find it when they search. At the start, one good page can be enough.

4
00:00:27.052 --> 00:00:27.652
What a first site needs

5
00:00:27.652 --> 00:00:39.352
Who and what: Who you are, what you are building, for whom and the difference you aim for. For example: Our bakery’s home page: “Good bread every Saturday, baked by young trainees.”

6
00:00:39.352 --> 00:00:48.459
Clear actions: Pages organised around what visitors need to do. For example: Buttons to order bread, refer a young person or support the bakery.

7
00:00:48.459 --> 00:00:58.307
Trust signals: Founders, your legal status or registration, and how you handle data. For example: An “About” section naming the founders, plus a short privacy note.

8
00:00:58.307 --> 00:01:09.726
Discoverability: Your audiences’ words, clear page titles, directory listings and partner links. For example: A free map listing and a link from the market’s stallholder page.

9
00:01:10.126 --> 00:01:10.726
Why it matters

10
00:01:10.726 --> 00:01:15.289
1. People check you online before they trust you.

11
00:01:15.289 --> 00:01:20.222
2. For something new, that first check matters even more.

12
00:01:20.222 --> 00:01:25.785
3. A clear page turns curiosity into a sign-up.

13
00:01:26.185 --> 00:01:26.785
What it connects to

14
00:01:26.785 --> 00:01:31.719
1. Your campaigns and posts send people here to act.

15
00:01:31.719 --> 00:01:35.911
2. Your trust signals and policies live here.

16
00:01:35.911 --> 00:01:41.844
3. Your measurement: forms and tracked links show what works.

17
00:01:42.244 --> 00:01:42.844
What to avoid

18
00:01:42.844 --> 00:01:47.407
Pages built around your structure, not visitors’ tasks.

19
00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:53.452
A site that is slow or hard to read on a phone.

20
00:01:53.452 --> 00:01:58.644
Search tricks instead of useful, accurate content.

21
00:01:59.244 --> 00:02:01.044
You plan your first site structure and discoverability actions.

22
00:02:01.044 --> 00:02:05.044
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:06.544 --> 00:02:09.644
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
